---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="American History & Heritage" description="Explore the history of the United States and the diverse histories, cultures, and living heritage of Native American nations.">
  <section class="heritage-hero"><div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">HISTORY · PEOPLES · HERITAGE</p>
    <h1>American History & Heritage</h1>
    <p class="lead">Explore the people, events, ideas, and encounters that shaped the United States — from the many Indigenous nations of North America to the country of today.</p>
    <p class="translation">История Соединённых Штатов и наследие народов, чья жизнь и культура формировались на этой земле задолго до появления страны.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container heritage-content">
    <a class="back-link" href="/american-english-method/">← Home</a>
    <p class="intro">A country is more than its founding documents and famous dates. Its history is also the history of the people who lived here, the communities they built, the cultures they preserved, and the difficult encounters that changed the continent. This section presents that story through careful, accessible explanations and clearly identified sources.</p>
    <p class="translation">История страны — это не только даты и документы. Это также история людей, их обществ, культур, встреч, конфликтов и перемен.</p>

    <div class="heritage-grid">
      <a class="heritage-card" href="#american-history">
        <span class="number">01 / HISTORY</span>
        <h2>American History</h2>
        <p>Follow the story of the United States from the world before European colonization to the present day.</p>
        <p class="ru">История США: от доколониальной Северной Америки до современности.</p>
        <span class="card-link">Explore the timeline ↓</span>
      </a>
      <a class="heritage-card" href="#native-nations">
        <span class="number">02 / INDIGENOUS HERITAGE</span>
        <h2>Native American Nations & Heritage</h2>
        <p>Meet distinct Indigenous nations, learn about their histories and traditions, and understand that Native communities are part of America today.</p>
        <p class="ru">Коренные народы: их история, культура, традиции и современная жизнь.</p>
        <span class="card-link">Explore Native heritage ↓</span>
      </a>
      <a class="heritage-card" href="#stories">
        <span class="number">03 / ORAL TRADITIONS</span>
        <h2>Legends, Stories & Epic Traditions</h2>
        <p>Discover storytelling traditions, cultural teachings, and literary works inspired by Indigenous narratives.</p>
        <p class="ru">Сказания, предания, устные традиции и литературные произведения.</p>
        <span class="card-link">Discover stories ↓</span>
      </a>
      <a class="heritage-card" href="/american-english-method/learn/culture-arts/">
        <span class="number">04 / CULTURE & ARTS</span>
        <h2>American Culture & Arts</h2>
        <p>Continue exploring American writers, poetry, visual art, music, film, and performing arts.</p>
        <p class="ru">Литература, поэзия, живопись, музыка, кино и театр.</p>
        <span class="card-link">Visit Culture & Arts ↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="heritage-section" id="american-history">
      <p class="eyebrow">A COUNTRY IN THE MAKING</p>
      <h2>American History</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">A chronological path through major periods and turning points. Each topic will become a standalone feature with a readable narrative, maps or images, a timeline, key terms, and questions for reflection.</p>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article><span>01</span><div><h3>North America Before Colonization</h3><p>The many societies, trade networks, cities, agricultural systems, and cultural worlds that existed long before the United States.</p><p class="ru">Северная Америка до колонизации: разнообразные общества, торговые пути, города и хозяйственные системы.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><h3>European Exploration & Colonization</h3><p>European expansion, the founding of colonies, encounters with Indigenous nations, cooperation, competition, and conflict.</p><p class="ru">Европейская экспансия, создание колоний и сложные отношения с коренными народами.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><h3>The American Revolution</h3><p>The struggle for independence, the Declaration of Independence, and the creation of a new political project.</p><p class="ru">Война за независимость и рождение нового государства.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Founding the United States</h3><p>The Constitution, the Bill of Rights, the early republic, and debates over the meaning of American ideals.</p><p class="ru">Конституция, Билль о правах и становление республики.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>05</span><div><h3>Expansion, Removal & the West</h3><p>Territorial expansion, migration, the forced removal of Native peoples, and the transformation of the continent.</p><p class="ru">Территориальное расширение, переселения, насильственное изгнание коренных народов и освоение Запада.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>06</span><div><h3>Slavery & the Civil War</h3><p>The history of slavery, resistance and abolition, the Civil War, emancipation, and Reconstruction.</p><p class="ru">Рабство, борьба за освобождение, Гражданская война и Реконструкция.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>07</span><div><h3>Industrialization & a Changing Nation</h3><p>Immigration, industrial growth, urban life, reform movements, and the emergence of the United States as a global power.</p><p class="ru">Иммиграция, индустриализация, рост городов и новые общественные движения.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>08</span><div><h3>America in the 20th Century</h3><p>Two world wars, the Great Depression, the Civil Rights Movement, the Cold War, and social change.</p><p class="ru">Мировые войны, Великая депрессия, движение за гражданские права и холодная война.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>09</span><div><h3>The United States Today</h3><p>Contemporary society, institutions, cultural diversity, technology, and America's place in the world.</p><p class="ru">Современное американское общество, институты, культура и роль США в мире.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="heritage-section" id="native-nations">
      <p class="eyebrow">MANY NATIONS · MANY HISTORIES</p>
      <h2>Native American Nations & Heritage</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">There was never one single Indigenous culture across North America. Hundreds of distinct nations developed their own languages, governments, economies, spiritual traditions, and relationships with the land. We will approach each nation on its own terms and, wherever possible, use sources created by Native scholars, cultural institutions, and communities.</p>
      <div class="native-grid">
        <article><h3>Peoples & Homelands</h3><p>Explore specific nations and the regions they call home, including their own names, languages, and histories.</p><p class="ru">Народы и территории: география, самоназвания, языки и исторические земли.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Life Before Colonization</h3><p>Learn about homes, food systems, farming, fishing, hunting, trade, craftsmanship, governance, and community life — with attention to regional differences.</p><p class="ru">Жилища, земледелие, охота, рыболовство, торговля, ремёсла и общественная жизнь.</p></article>
        <article><h3>First Encounters & Colonial Relations</h3><p>Study diplomacy, alliances, trade, disease, warfare, treaties, land dispossession, and forced removal without reducing complex histories to a single narrative.</p><p class="ru">Дипломатия, торговля, союзы, эпидемии, войны, договоры и потеря земель.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Culture, Knowledge & Traditions</h3><p>Discover languages, art, music, ecological knowledge, oral histories, and cultural practices, while respecting community protocols around sacred or restricted knowledge.</p><p class="ru">Языки, искусство, музыка, знания о природе и культурные традиции.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Native Nations Today</h3><p>Meet contemporary Native communities, tribal governments, language revitalization projects, artists, educators, and leaders.</p><p class="ru">Современные сообщества, племенное самоуправление, возрождение языков и культурная жизнь.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Names, Maps & Historical Sources</h3><p>Explain historical terminology, changing borders, treaties, and the difference between outside descriptions and Indigenous perspectives.</p><p class="ru">Исторические названия, карты, договоры и взгляд самих коренных народов.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="editorial-note"><strong>Our approach:</strong> Native nations are living peoples, not merely subjects of the past. We will avoid treating them as one group, presenting stereotypes as facts, or using sacred stories without checking whether they are appropriate to share.</div>
    </section>

    <section class="heritage-section" id="stories">
      <p class="eyebrow">STORIES THAT CARRY CULTURE</p>
      <h2>Legends, Oral Traditions & Literature</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Stories can preserve history, values, humour, relationships with the natural world, and ways of understanding life. We will distinguish community oral traditions from later literary adaptations and identify who recorded, translated, or retold each work.</p>
      <div class="story-feature">
        <div><span class="number">FEATURED LITERARY CONNECTION</span><h3>The Song of Hiawatha</h3><p>Henry Wadsworth Longfellow's 1855 poem drew on material associated with Ojibwe traditions, including accounts mediated through earlier collectors. It is an influential work of American literature, but it should not be presented as a verbatim Indigenous epic or as a complete account of Ojibwe beliefs.</p><p class="ru">«Песнь о Гайавате» — литературная поэма Генри Лонгфелло, основанная на мотивах, связанных с традициями оджибве. Важно отличать авторское произведение XIX века от подлинной устной традиции народа оджибве.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="editorial-note"><strong>Respect and accuracy matter.</strong> Some stories are intended for particular seasons, audiences, ceremonies, or community settings. We will prioritize versions that communities have made available for public learning and provide attribution and cultural context.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="learning-box">
      <p class="eyebrow">LEARN THROUGH HISTORY</p>
      <h2>English and historical understanding, together.</h2>
      <p>Each feature will connect cultural knowledge with language learning: an accessible English narrative, Russian support, a vocabulary guide, a timeline or visual source, audio when available, and questions that encourage learners to explain what they have understood.</p>
      <p class="ru">Каждая публикация будет помогать не только узнавать историю, но и развивать английский: текст, перевод, словарь, наглядные материалы, аудио и вопросы для обсуждения.</p>
      <div class="learning-steps"><span>Discover</span><span>Understand</span><span>Learn the language</span><span>Discuss</span></div>
    </section>
    <p class="source-note">Historical and cultural features will be developed from reliable sources, including primary documents, museums, archives, universities, and Native-led cultural institutions. Sources and image credits will be identified in individual articles.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.heritage-hero{padding:78px 0 84px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0d1929,#1b304a);color:#fffefa}
.heritage-hero .container,.heritage-content{max-width:1040px}
.eyebrow{color:#c5a267;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em}
h1{margin:18px 0;font:600 clamp(40px,6vw,64px)/1.1 "Playfair Display",serif}
.lead{max-width:850px;color:#e0e4e9;font-size:20px;line-height:1.7}
.translation,.ru{color:#89929d;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7}
.heritage-hero .translation{color:#c5cdd6}
.heritage-content{padding-top:34px;padding-bottom:80px}
.intro{max-width:920px;margin-top:30px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;color:#26364a}
.heritage-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin-top:36px}
.heritage-card{display:block;padding:26px;border:1px solid #e2ded5;background:#fffefa;transition:background .2s,border-color .2s}
.heritage-card:hover{background:#fbf8f0;border-color:#b89552}
.number{color:#b89552;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em}
.heritage-card h2{margin:12px 0;color:#172538;font:600 25px "Playfair Display",serif}
.heritage-card p,.heritage-section p{color:#465363;line-height:1.75}
.heritage-card .ru{color:#89929d;font-size:13px}
.card-link{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;color:#8b6b32;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
.heritage-section{margin-top:76px;scroll-margin-top:30px}
.heritage-section>h2,.learning-box h2{margin:12px 0 16px;color:#172538;font:600 clamp(30px,4vw,38px)/1.2 "Playfair Display",serif}
.section-lead{max-width:920px;font-size:16px}
.timeline{margin-top:30px;border-top:1px solid #e2ded5}
.timeline article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:54px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:21px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #e2ded5}
.timeline article>span{color:#b89552;font:600 22px "Playfair Display",serif}
.timeline h3,.native-grid h3,.story-feature h3{margin:0 0 8px;color:#172538;font:600 22px "Playfair Display",serif}
.timeline p{margin:6px 0;font-size:14px}
.timeline .ru{font-size:13px;color:#89929d}
.native-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:28px}
.native-grid article{padding:23px;border:1px solid #e2ded5;background:#fffefa}
.native-grid p{margin:8px 0;font-size:14px}
.native-grid .ru{font-size:13px;color:#89929d}
.editorial-note{margin-top:22px;padding:19px 22px;border-left:3px solid #b89552;background:#f4f1eb;color:#465363;font-size:14px;line-height:1.75}
.story-feature{margin-top:26px;padding:28px;border:1px solid #e2ded5;background:#fffefa}
.story-feature h3{margin-top:12px;font-size:28px}
.story-feature p{font-size:15px}
.story-feature .ru{color:#89929d;font-size:14px}
.learning-box{margin-top:70px;padding:34px;background:#0d1929;color:#fffefa}
.learning-box h2{color:#fffefa}
.learning-box>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:900px;color:#d7dce2;line-height:1.8}
.learning-box .ru{color:#c5cdd6}
.learning-steps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:24px}
.learning-steps span{padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid rgba(232,220,193,.4);color:#e8dcc1;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
.source-note{margin-top:26px;color:#89929d;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7}
@media(max-width:700px){.heritage-grid,.native-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.heritage-hero{padding:58px 0}.heritage-section{margin-top:56px}.timeline article{grid-template-columns:38px 1fr;gap:10px}.learning-box{padding:24px}}
</style>
